# Project context — Durpalla driver app (Android)

## Map
- `app/src/main/java/com/durpalla/driver/`: `MainActivity.kt`, `DriverApplication.kt` (entry);
  `ui/nav/` (AppNav, NavActions — all Back-to-Home logic), `ui/screens/`, `ui/components/` (Buttons: `DurpallaButton`, `DurpallaFab`…), `ui/theme/Theme.kt`, `ui/DriverViewModel.kt`;
  `data/` (`Repositories.kt`, `ApiJson.kt`, mock data in `FakeData.kt`); `domain/` (Models, Rules, Format);
  `call/` (WebRTC + Firestore signaling, `CallApi.kt`, `AudioQuality.kt`); `realtime/` (Pusher); `notifications/` (FCM); `i18n/` (AppLanguage, `Digits.kt`, UiText); `security/BotProtection.kt`.
- Config: `app/build.gradle.kts`, `gradle/libs.versions.toml`, `app/google-services.json.example`. Docs: `docs/`, README (calling contract).
- Tests: `app/src/test/…` (unit + Roborazzi screenshot tests).

## Commands
- Build: `./gradlew :app:assembleDebug`
- Targeted test: `./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest --tests "*DigitFormatterTest"`
- Avoid full screenshot runs unless UI changed.

## Conventions
- Brand teal/blue `#0E5F7E` family (see `ui/theme/Theme.kt`); use `DurpallaButton` / brand components.
- Bangla + English via resources/UiText; Bangla digits for display (`i18n/Digits.kt`), ASCII to the API.
- Navigation: Done/Close/Back to Home must go to a clean Home (use NavActions).
- Backend: `durpalla-apigw` under `/api/v1/driver/`; currently uses FakeData until the real client lands.
